{"id": "d6a326a7-ba39-43ef-9af8-e8d330e578b2", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll scan SageMaker notebook instances and Studio domains in parallel across your associated accounts and regions. It's a read-only check of network exposure and encryption settings.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_nIARiwPBHNtySqfw9wa07P", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sm-notebook-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["discovering-topology"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only security audit of ALL SageMaker notebook instances for internet exposure and encryption at rest.",
  "context": "User asked to audit SageMaker notebooks and domains. You cover NOTEBOOK INSTANCES only; another sub-agent covers Studio domains. Use only read-only (list/describe/get) calls. Agent space account is 012345678901_1, region us-east-1. Use list_associations to find every associated AWS account, then scan all enabled regions (use ec2 describe_regions or at least every region where SageMaker is available) in each account. Skip regions/accounts that error with access denied, and report them as coverage gaps.",
  "resources": ["sagemaker list_notebook_instances / describe_notebook_instance", "ec2 describe_security_groups / describe_subnets / describe_route_tables / describe_network_interfaces", "kms describe_key"],
  "criteria": "For each notebook instance report: name, account, region, status, DirectInternetAccess (Enabled = internet exposure), SubnetId and whether the subnet routes to an internet gateway or auto-assigns public IPs, attached security groups with any inbound rules open to 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0, RootAccess, KmsKeyId for the ML storage volume (absent = AWS-managed/default key; if present note whether customer-managed and whether rotation is enabled), and whether the instance sits in a VPC at all. Rate each finding High/Medium/Low with a one-line reason. Return a concise summary: totals scanned, a table of findings, clean instances count, coverage gaps, and short remediation notes. Do not attempt any changes."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit SageMaker notebook instances for exposure and encryption"}, {"id": "tooluse_R0kqyZQ47B6E3kj6K9OS1S", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sm-domain-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["discovering-topology"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only security audit of ALL SageMaker (Studio) domains for internet exposure and encryption at rest.",
  "context": "User asked to audit SageMaker notebooks and domains. You cover SAGEMAKER DOMAINS only; another sub-agent covers notebook instances. Use only read-only (list/describe/get) calls. Agent space account is 012345678901_1, region us-east-1. Use list_associations to find every associated AWS account, then scan all enabled regions (use ec2 describe_regions or at least every region where SageMaker is available) in each account. Skip regions/accounts that error with access denied, and report them as coverage gaps.",
  "resources": ["sagemaker list_domains / describe_domain / list_user_profiles / list_spaces", "ec2 describe_security_groups / describe_subnets / describe_route_tables / describe_vpc_endpoints", "kms describe_key"],
  "criteria": "For each domain report: domain id/name, account, region, status, AppNetworkAccessType (PublicInternetOnly = internet egress exposure, VpcOnly = good), subnets and whether they route to an internet gateway/NAT, security groups (note inbound rules open to 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0, and the domain-boundary security groups), whether VPC endpoints exist for SageMaker API/runtime/Studio when VpcOnly, AuthMode, KmsKeyId for the home EFS volume (absent = AWS-managed key; if present note customer-managed and rotation status), and any default user settings or space settings that relax security (e.g., direct internet / root access on Jupyter apps where visible, sharing settings). Rate each finding High/Medium/Low with a one-line reason. Return a concise summary: totals scanned, a table of findings, clean domains count, coverage gaps, and short remediation notes. Do not attempt any changes."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit SageMaker domains for exposure and encryption"}], "created_at": null}

